turnip (guamp A610): TU_GUAMP_GMEM=fetch|blur (tile memory for the framebuffer-fetch passes, and for Turnip-owned passes that load
nothing), exact tile stores also where the aligned rows would leave an image that shares its memory (a plane of a planar IOSurface
imported whole, a texture over a buffer at an offset), and counter [7]: passes in sysmem with SINGLE_PRIM_MODE

metal2vulkan reads Metal's framebuffer fetch as input attachments in rasterization order; in sysmem Turnip draws such a pipeline with
GRAS_SC_CNTL FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP_AND_OVERWRITE (the CCU written back to DRAM at every overlap), in GMEM with FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP on chip
and the input read from tile memory. fetch = msaa + those passes (the autotune then picks GMEM for them); blur = fetch + passes whose
attachments are all Turnip's own and cleared or don't-care (Core Animation's blur and offscreen passes), left to the autotune.
0003 checked the fast store only against the end of the BO: the bridge imports a planar surface whole ('b3a8' 750x1666: BGR10 XR
plane then the A8 plane), so the two rows past 1666 (6 KiB of tile garbage) land inside the BO, at the start of the next plane.
Policy values 0-3 unchanged (row TU pol 4 fetch, 5 blur; f<counter 7> with adreno-metal 0055). Applies after 0001-0003 (both 0003).

